## Brand and writing source decisions

The [brand inventory](../reference/brand-guidance.json) maps the four requested Brand sections and their linked guidance to local rules. The official graphic device, logo system and brand-in-use sections are excluded from this work package.

The [writing inventory](../reference/writing-guide.json) records the reviewed chapters, local rules, exclusions and source conflicts for:

- [NHS content guidance](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/content): user needs, plain language, interface content and inclusion.
- [Home Office content style guide](https://design.homeoffice.gov.uk/design-and-content/content/content-style-guide): consistent terminology and accessible public-facing content.
- [GOV.UK publishing writing guidelines](https://guidance.publishing.service.gov.uk/writing-to-gov-uk-standards/writing-guidelines/): clear language, structure, tone and editorial work.
- [Plain English Campaign free guides](https://www.plainenglish.co.uk/free-guides): clear explanations, forms, layout and proofreading. The four reviewed guide titles are recorded in the inventory; the PDFs remain with their publisher.
- [SCULPT](https://www.worcestershire.gov.uk/council-services/business/digital-worcestershire/sculpt-accessibility/what-sculpt): an accessibility review prompt developed by Helen Wilson at Worcestershire County Council.

These sources inform original household rules and examples. We do not copy their organisational workflows or claim endorsement. The [writing guide](../content/index.html) explains how to resolve conflicting advice; [licensing](licensing.html) records the separate source-material terms.

## Local sources

- `design-system/palettes.json`: canonical supplied palette specification.
- `design-system/themes.json`: resolved theme-variable mapping.
- `brand/civica/`: supplied V3.2 asset pack, proof, palette variants and provenance records.
- `docs/source/reference/brand-assets.json`: published artwork source mapping and hashes.
- `docs/source/design-contract.json`: machine-readable local rules.
- `docs/source/llms.txt`: reading order for agents and automated tooling.
- [Visual audit sources](../reference/visual-audit-sources.json): reviewed official code commits and file hashes for border, icon and badge decisions.

The [visual review](visual-audit.html) explains how the public homepage, reusable Design System and native Home Assistant interface differ. Do not treat a homepage screenshot as a specification for every control.

## Verify claims at the right level

A source's accessibility findings apply to its tested implementation, not automatically to civica.uk. The supplied asset pack's verification record describes its mechanical checks; it does not establish live Home Assistant compatibility or government approval.

Record source changes during maintenance and update the [deviation register](deviations.html), implementation and tests together.
